WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.961
- Have you ever thought about rapping?

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:06.172
- What made you ask me that?

00:00:07.382 --> 00:00:08.883
- His size. 
This is not for me.

00:00:08.883 --> 00:00:10.135
- Yeah.
-  I am not a 13!

00:00:10.135 --> 00:00:11.094
- Yeah, I need it.
- [Laughing]

00:00:11.845 --> 00:00:16.558
When the Raptors traded you, 
did you feel more hurt or more angry?

00:00:16.558 --> 00:00:17.517
- I…

00:00:18.643 --> 00:00:23.356
[♪♪♪]

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:26.568
- [Announcer]: It’s off to Leonard, 
defended by Simmons. 

00:00:26.568 --> 00:00:28.153
Is this the dagger?

00:00:28.153 --> 00:00:29.154
[Buzzer sounding]

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:33.992
- Ohhh!
- [Cheering]

00:00:33.992 --> 00:00:37.203
- The big storyline during the playoffs 
now has kinda been, like,

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:40.290
“What’s DeMar thinking 
watching the Raptors playing?” 

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:41.916
So what is DeMar thinking?

00:00:41.916 --> 00:00:42.917
- Um, 

00:00:42.917 --> 00:00:45.503
people gotta understand, like, 
my best friend is Kyle.

00:00:45.503 --> 00:00:46.796
- [Announcer]: Career high for Kyle Lowry!

00:00:46.796 --> 00:00:49.924
- So, I’m rootin’ for my best friend, 
you know,

00:00:49.924 --> 00:00:54.387
to do well, to accomplish something 
that we tried to do all those years,

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:55.930
and he has the opportunity to do it.

00:00:57.348 --> 00:01:01.895
Some guys on the team, 
they know, you know, I’m rootin’ for ‘em.

00:01:03.772 --> 00:01:07.567
- I know that now this narrative is, like, 
“They couldn’t get there with DeMar.”

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:09.319
“They can only get there 
now cuz they have Kawhi.”

00:01:09.319 --> 00:01:12.447
- Mhmm.
- What is your response to that?

00:01:12.447 --> 00:01:16.534
- Honestly, I don’t even think I said this—
I probably said this to my own inner circle—

00:01:16.534 --> 00:01:19.829
but if it wasn’t for all the years and groundwork
that I did before then, 

00:01:19.829 --> 00:01:21.664
none of them things would’ve been possible.

00:01:21.664 --> 00:01:23.500
Yes, I fought. 
I sacrificed. 

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:26.628
I pushed the limits to where 
I had to be the sacrificial lamb.

00:01:26.628 --> 00:01:29.380
You just have to sit back and understand,
like, you know,

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:33.718
you are the reason so many things 
was even possible. 

00:01:33.718 --> 00:01:37.430
- [Announcer]: It’s up and good! With 1.9 remaining.

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:41.267
- To their credit, 
they probably felt like it was time to see

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:44.104
what we could get to make that next jump.

00:01:47.315 --> 00:01:51.694
- When the Raptors traded you, 
did you feel more hurt or more angry?

00:01:51.694 --> 00:01:59.410
- More hurt, because, you know, 
being invested from 19 to—I was, what, 28?

00:01:59.410 --> 00:02:01.663
You know, everything you learn was from there.

00:02:01.663 --> 00:02:03.706
Everything you gained was from there.

00:02:03.706 --> 00:02:06.042
So for that—[snapping fingers]—to be gone like that

00:02:06.042 --> 00:02:08.878
when you least expect it, 
it just throws you off guard.

00:02:08.878 --> 00:02:11.840
You know, we human at the end 
of the day and it, it definitely hits you.

00:02:13.591 --> 00:02:15.718
- Now, you’re in San Antonio.
- Mhmm.

00:02:15.718 --> 00:02:20.223
- Playin’ with the Spurs. 
Most importantly, playin’ for Popovich.

00:02:20.223 --> 00:02:25.562
- Pop is cool. He’s like a Don Corleone.

00:02:25.728 --> 00:02:28.398
You know, he makes you look at him not just

00:02:28.398 --> 00:02:32.026
like the basketball coach, 
but like, you know, a great individual.

00:02:32.026 --> 00:02:34.612
And I called him the other day just to talk, 
talk trash to him,

00:02:34.612 --> 00:02:37.991
and he not good with workin’ 
the iPhones and all that.

00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:41.244
Like, he hates technology to a passion, 
so he always

00:02:41.244 --> 00:02:45.415
talk about he gonna put somethin’ on Twitter, 
like, knowin’ he ain’t got a Twitter.

00:02:45.415 --> 00:02:47.375
- Mhmm.
- Like, you know, he called it Twittergram.

00:02:47.375 --> 00:02:50.587
“I’mma put somethin’ on Twittergram 
and see if they catch this,”

00:02:50.587 --> 00:02:52.255
and somethin’ like, just stuff like that.

00:02:52.255 --> 00:02:53.882
- Twittergram, the newest app.
- Yeah.

00:02:54.716 --> 00:02:58.720
- Gimme an example of something 
he educated you guys on in a meeting.

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:01.347
- I remember one meeting, 
I’m thinkin’ we were gonna watch film.

00:03:01.347 --> 00:03:03.558
He put on a penguin movie.

00:03:03.558 --> 00:03:03.975
It was the most crazy—

00:03:03.975 --> 00:03:04.726
- Like, “The March—”

00:03:04.726 --> 00:03:07.020
- Like, the whole thing from, 
you know, having a baby,

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:09.939
to the male carrying the egg, to the women go out,

00:03:09.939 --> 00:03:11.983
fish for food, bring back the food.

00:03:11.983 --> 00:03:16.070
Two months later, 
penguins walk 90 miles with the egg.

00:03:16.070 --> 00:03:22.452
The whole point of it was how 
life is a full circle, you know,

00:03:22.452 --> 00:03:26.664
and how we all—as long as we work 
together and stick together and stay

00:03:26.664 --> 00:03:30.710
on the same track, how we could 
accomplish the most impossible mission.

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:36.507
- I remember reading he will spend tons of 
money on team dinners throughout the season.

00:03:36.507 --> 00:03:38.801
- Mandatory. 
He called it “break bread.”

00:03:38.801 --> 00:03:40.887
Win, lose or draw, after a game,

00:03:40.887 --> 00:03:43.473
if we stayin’ over in a city, we got a team dinner.

00:03:43.473 --> 00:03:46.726
We goin’ to break bread, we gonna have 
a good night, a good evening.

00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:48.186
You know, we’re family.

00:03:48.186 --> 00:03:51.648
[♪♪♪]

00:03:51.648 --> 00:03:53.983
- Let’s go buy some shoes!
- Get it!

00:03:55.818 --> 00:03:56.819
So this the spot.

00:03:57.862 --> 00:03:59.072
- Is it like heaven?

00:03:59.989 --> 00:04:00.448
- It’s everything.

00:04:00.448 --> 00:04:01.407
- Ahhhh.

00:04:01.407 --> 00:04:03.952
- You know, this, this my go-to spot

00:04:03.952 --> 00:04:07.247
- You come in here, there’s a lotta shoes. 
Where do you start?

00:04:08.289 --> 00:04:11.000
- Sometimes I think about my favorite Jordans,

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:13.920
which ones I don’t have or I can’t find, 
and I come in here

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:16.506
and look for ‘em and see what they got, like—

00:04:16.506 --> 00:04:18.549
- Which Jordans stick out to you up here?

00:04:18.549 --> 00:04:27.058
- Hmmm, what Jordans, to me, 
I feel like I need? Probably these.

00:04:27.058 --> 00:04:29.811
The Shattered Backboards.

00:04:29.811 --> 00:04:33.731
- What about those? 
Like, what makes those stick out?

00:04:33.731 --> 00:04:35.650
- Cuz I don’t think I have these.

00:04:36.526 --> 00:04:39.320
- How many sneakers do you have?
The real number.

00:04:40.405 --> 00:04:44.033
- That’s a great question. 
Um, I play in a different shoe every single game,

00:04:44.033 --> 00:04:48.204
so I probably go through at least 
100 pairs of shoes in a season.

00:04:48.204 --> 00:04:50.373
- Yeah.
- Every single game, I play in new shoes.

00:04:50.373 --> 00:04:54.043
My shoes at home, 
it’s definitely at a couple hundred. 

00:04:54.043 --> 00:04:55.295
Probably, uh—

00:04:55.295 --> 00:04:57.588
- More than two?
- For sure.

00:04:57.588 --> 00:04:59.215
- More than four?
- Yeah.

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:02.760
- More than 600?
- Probably up there for sure.

00:05:04.721 --> 00:05:07.515
- Are there any shoes that, 
like, take you to a specific

00:05:07.515 --> 00:05:09.684
memory or a specific game 
when you look at ‘em?

00:05:10.601 --> 00:05:12.437
- These were the fake Jordans I had.

00:05:13.062 --> 00:05:14.564
- Those are the ones your dad got you?

00:05:14.564 --> 00:05:15.606
- Yeah, the 13s.

00:05:15.606 --> 00:05:16.607
- How’d you know they were fake?

00:05:16.607 --> 00:05:20.069
- With the Jumpman the other way, 
and I poked a hole in a bubble.

00:05:20.069 --> 00:05:22.530
The Jordan was fake, everything, like, with these—

00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:24.949
- But it’s great cuz I know you still loved ‘em.

00:05:24.949 --> 00:05:26.200
- Oh, yeah, without a doubt.

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:29.871
I wore ‘em. I wore ‘em till 
they had a hole in ‘em, literally.

00:05:32.498 --> 00:05:35.376
I like these. 
I might get these.

00:05:35.376 --> 00:05:36.336
These are awesome.

00:05:36.336 --> 00:05:38.504
- And so you don’t even have to 
try ‘em on, you just know?

00:05:38.504 --> 00:05:40.048
- Nah, nah. 
Yeah, I know my feet.

00:05:43.051 --> 00:05:43.760
Nope.

00:05:44.844 --> 00:05:48.014
- Now, when you say that you 
wear a new shoe every game,

00:05:48.014 --> 00:05:50.933
do you mean new, 
never been worn, or new—?

00:05:50.933 --> 00:05:52.101
- Never been worn. 
Brand new.

00:05:52.852 --> 00:05:53.728
- OK, explain why.

00:05:54.187 --> 00:05:58.858
- I don’t tie my shoes when I play. 
Like, I do not lace my shoes at all.

00:05:58.858 --> 00:06:01.069
I like my shoes tight-fit.

00:06:01.069 --> 00:06:04.822
So when they’re brand new, 
they fit my feet perfectly.

00:06:04.822 --> 00:06:07.700
So once I play, my shoe’s broken into,

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:09.369
I’m done with them shoes.

00:06:09.369 --> 00:06:10.328
Need a new one next game.

00:06:11.913 --> 00:06:13.456
- What size shoe are you?
- 13.

00:06:13.456 --> 00:06:15.333
- Do you guys have this in a 13?

00:06:17.543 --> 00:06:19.504
His size. 
This is not for me.

00:06:19.504 --> 00:06:20.505
-  I am not a 13!

00:06:20.505 --> 00:06:22.131
- Yeah, I need it if you got ‘em for me.

00:06:22.131 --> 00:06:24.509
I walk around in a 13; 
I hoop in a 14.

00:06:25.134 --> 00:06:26.469
- Well, I’m happy that I know now.

00:06:26.803 --> 00:06:28.930
- Yeah.
What would you get?

00:06:28.930 --> 00:06:30.932
- What I’d get, I don’t think is over here.
I think it’s over here.

00:06:30.932 --> 00:06:31.891
- All right.
- OK.

00:06:31.891 --> 00:06:33.142
- Let’s take a look over here.

00:06:33.768 --> 00:06:35.395
I have every Kobe in the world.

00:06:35.395 --> 00:06:37.313
- You really have every single Kobe shoe?

00:06:37.313 --> 00:06:39.440
- Yeah, I have every single Kobe shoe.

00:06:40.274 --> 00:06:44.487
- Talk to me about what Kobe has 
meant to you, cuz I know that’s a very,

00:06:44.487 --> 00:06:48.741
like, key figure in your basketball life.

00:06:48.741 --> 00:06:53.454
- Kob was somebody I just gravitated 
to and always rooted for.

00:06:53.454 --> 00:06:57.291
I remember his rookie year when 
he was, when he played at Utah

00:06:57.291 --> 00:07:00.586
and he air-balled all them threes, and, you know,

00:07:00.586 --> 00:07:01.629
I remember everybody killin’ him.

00:07:01.629 --> 00:07:05.258
And, I don’t know, I just 
remember being emotional as a kid.

00:07:05.258 --> 00:07:06.342
Like, “Damn, why they doin’ that? 
Why they doin’ that?”

00:07:07.093 --> 00:07:08.010
- “You doin’ my dawg like that.”

00:07:08.010 --> 00:07:10.221
- Yeah, man, like, this my 
favorite player, and it just grew

00:07:10.221 --> 00:07:14.142
over time to where that was my 
favorite player to bein’ able to

00:07:14.142 --> 00:07:17.061
have a relationship with him, 
to be able to play against him.

00:07:17.562 --> 00:07:19.147
- Now Kobe, of course, was a Laker.

00:07:20.189 --> 00:07:23.109
- Do you ever have any dreams of playing in L.A.?

00:07:23.109 --> 00:07:26.320
- I think you’d be crazy to say 
you never wanted to play at home.

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:30.199
Everybody always wanna have 
the opportunity, but I think 

00:07:30.199 --> 00:07:34.871
I’m definitely happy where I’m at, 
and I’ll watch ‘em from a distance.

00:07:36.164 --> 00:07:40.418
- What do you love more, shoes or music?

00:07:40.418 --> 00:07:42.336
And you have to pick. 
Don’t say both.

00:07:43.087 --> 00:07:44.714
- Music.
- Really?

00:07:44.714 --> 00:07:47.508
- Yeah, music. 
I think for me, I need that constant

00:07:47.508 --> 00:07:50.803
new music of something you can relate to.

00:07:50.803 --> 00:07:54.348
You need it. You need it 
for every and any type of mood.

00:07:54.348 --> 00:07:56.058
- What’d you listen to on your way to the interview?

00:07:56.058 --> 00:07:56.934
- Nipsey.

00:07:56.934 --> 00:07:57.560
- Nipsey.

00:07:57.560 --> 00:08:01.397
- Nipsey Hussle. 
Old, new, whatever, just Nip in rotation.

00:08:02.523 --> 00:08:04.942
- Grammy-nominated rapper and community activist

00:08:04.942 --> 00:08:06.527
Nipsey Hussle was murdered

00:08:06.527 --> 00:08:08.988
in broad daylight outside a clothing store

00:08:08.988 --> 00:08:10.698
that he owned in South Los Angeles.

00:08:10.698 --> 00:08:13.075
And he was killed just before he was about to meet

00:08:13.075 --> 00:08:15.578
with city leaders and the LAPD

00:08:15.578 --> 00:08:16.578
about reducing gang violence.

00:08:19.123 --> 00:08:21.375
- [Rooks]: What made him so special to you?

00:08:21.375 --> 00:08:25.463
- [DeRozan]: I grew up in Compton. 
Roughest of the rough.

00:08:25.463 --> 00:08:28.466
To us comin’ from the urban area, you know,

00:08:28.466 --> 00:08:31.469
we seen a guy like Nipsey start from nothin’.

00:08:32.386 --> 00:08:33.679
You know, he was our motivation.

00:08:33.679 --> 00:08:38.226
He was a different type of light for 
us that we could, we could relate to.

00:08:38.226 --> 00:08:42.313
We understood, and there’s a lotta 
people I’m close to that still live there.

00:08:42.313 --> 00:08:46.943
People gettin’ killed, people gettin’—
it’s so much of that reality that’s my reality.

00:08:48.277 --> 00:08:51.697
The crazy thing, I think it was about two 
or three weeks before, I had dinner with him.

00:08:51.697 --> 00:08:54.742
We had the most in-depth 
conversations about, you know, life.

00:08:54.742 --> 00:08:57.578
About how to be a better individual.

00:08:57.578 --> 00:09:01.207
How to, you know, give back. 
How to make sure your people straight.

00:09:01.207 --> 00:09:03.084
A plan to do something great.

00:09:03.084 --> 00:09:05.294
That’s something that’s always gonna, 
you know, I’mma stick,

00:09:05.294 --> 00:09:09.799
stick close to me for sure because I 
remember that night like it was yesterday.

00:09:11.842 --> 00:09:15.179
- So have you ever thought about rapping?

00:09:18.140 --> 00:09:20.560
- Oh my god. 
[Sighing]

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:23.479
I mean, did somebody tell you something?

00:09:23.479 --> 00:09:26.691
- I just wanna know the answer. 
This is, I’m asking you the questions.

00:09:26.691 --> 00:09:30.528
- All right, this is, this is another exclusive 
that I’mma say here on your show.

00:09:30.528 --> 00:09:32.905
- OK.
- Only people close to me know, know this.

00:09:34.907 --> 00:09:37.952
But I have, like, an album/mixtape.

00:09:37.952 --> 00:09:41.664
- Tell me about this album/mixtape, OK?!

00:09:41.664 --> 00:09:43.499
Could we get a track?
- Oh, man.

00:09:44.542 --> 00:09:47.128
You know, the last two summers, 
honestly, I been thinkin’ about,

00:09:47.128 --> 00:09:49.297
like, just leakin’ a song and see what happens.

00:09:49.297 --> 00:09:52.300
- OK, tell me one lyric you’ve written you love.

00:09:52.925 --> 00:09:55.303
Just one! 
You gotta give us a taste!

00:09:55.303 --> 00:09:56.887
- Yo, you settin’ me up!

00:09:58.681 --> 00:10:00.891
- One lyric. 
Something from a song.

00:10:00.891 --> 00:10:03.728
- I’m tryna find any way to get outta 
this right now, I ain’t gonna lie.

00:10:03.728 --> 00:10:05.605
I’m just tryin’ to make up somethin’, like—

00:10:06.147 --> 00:10:08.274
- Cuz this is the thing, everyone’s about to know.

00:10:08.274 --> 00:10:10.735
This is gonna be on Bleacher Report. 
They gonna know you rap.

00:10:10.735 --> 00:10:15.239
OK, if you had to pick a rapper—
I’m not saying you sound like them,

00:10:15.239 --> 00:10:19.660
but you think that your sound is maybe similar?

00:10:20.161 --> 00:10:21.996
- I don’t know. 
It’s just me, like, you know,

00:10:21.996 --> 00:10:23.706
West Coast Compton sound.

00:10:23.706 --> 00:10:25.374
I’ve gotten Ice Cube.

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:27.001
- OK!
- Yeah.

00:10:27.001 --> 00:10:30.546
I’d had a few of my rapper friends, 
like, kinda compliment me,

00:10:30.546 --> 00:10:32.465
so it gave me a little bit more confidence.

00:10:32.465 --> 00:10:34.467
- What rappers have complimented your music?

00:10:34.467 --> 00:10:37.303
- I let Kendrick hear one of my songs before.

00:10:37.303 --> 00:10:38.304
I let Drake hear.

00:10:42.475 --> 00:10:44.852
You about to have me go viral about bein’ a rapper.

00:10:44.852 --> 00:10:45.603
- It’s gonna be great.

00:10:45.603 --> 00:10:47.355
- Oh my god.
- It’s gonna be so great.

00:10:47.355 --> 00:10:48.522
- I never thought the day would come.

00:10:48.522 --> 00:10:50.399
- Then just gotta make it my ringtone.

00:10:52.860 --> 00:10:53.944
DeMar’s song will be my ringtone.

00:10:53.944 --> 00:10:57.031
- Oh, I’mma be gettin’ tagged in so much stuff.

00:10:57.031 --> 00:10:59.241
- What were Drake’s critiques of your rap?

00:10:59.241 --> 00:11:01.744
- I was at one of his shows. 
He played it in the back.

00:11:01.744 --> 00:11:04.330
Everybody was back there, and he played it.

00:11:04.330 --> 00:11:07.041
And everybody—only he knew it was me.

00:11:07.041 --> 00:11:07.541
- Yeah.

00:11:07.541 --> 00:11:10.878
- But everybody was like—

00:11:10.878 --> 00:11:12.880
“I don’t even know who you 
are anymore, DeMar.” 

00:11:12.880 --> 00:11:15.716
Like, what are you talking about?

00:11:16.092 --> 00:11:18.177
- Wait, but so everyone’s listening to it, 
didn’t know it was you,

00:11:18.177 --> 00:11:18.886
but they liked the song?

00:11:18.886 --> 00:11:20.096
- Yeah, you know what I mean, but—

00:11:20.096 --> 00:11:20.930
- You felt good, though.

00:11:20.930 --> 00:11:21.806
- No, I felt good.

00:11:21.806 --> 00:11:23.933
- Yeah.
- I was cool with that, like, my dawgs—

00:11:23.933 --> 00:11:26.227
nobody else need to hear this. 
I’m cool.

00:11:28.813 --> 00:11:33.693
- Now, in 2018, you publicly 
acknowledged depression by tweeting,

00:11:33.693 --> 00:11:36.028
“This depression gets the best of me.”

00:11:36.028 --> 00:11:36.404
- Mhmm.

00:11:36.404 --> 00:11:38.948
- When it gets the best of you, 
what does that look like?

00:11:39.365 --> 00:11:41.409
- You know, everything just build up at once.

00:11:41.409 --> 00:11:44.954
You know, you kinda shut 
yourself out from everything.

00:11:44.954 --> 00:11:46.956
A lotta people don’t understand, you know,

00:11:46.956 --> 00:11:51.293
and you kinda could be around a 
group of people and still feel alone.

00:11:51.293 --> 00:11:56.006
- What was going on for you personally 
at that moment that you sent that tweet?

00:11:56.006 --> 00:11:59.176
- I think it was an overwhelming of everything.

00:11:59.176 --> 00:12:01.387
When I tweeted, that was 
All-Star Weekend in L.A.,

00:12:01.387 --> 00:12:06.225
and being in L.A., being a 
starter on the All-Star team.

00:12:06.225 --> 00:12:10.229
I’m just excited to get home, 
wanna see my kids, wanna chill.

00:12:10.229 --> 00:12:13.190
Everything just became so overwhelming,

00:12:13.190 --> 00:12:14.608
you know, and I just had that moment.

00:12:14.608 --> 00:12:18.696
You know, I turned to Twitter, 
which is the devil.

00:12:20.322 --> 00:12:22.491
- So when you sent it, though, you’re like,

00:12:22.491 --> 00:12:24.744
“OK, this feels good”? Did you get nervous?

00:12:24.744 --> 00:12:26.787
- Yeah, in the moment. 
I didn’t think nothin’ other than,

00:12:26.787 --> 00:12:29.957
“What have I done? 
Now I gotta deal with this head-on.”

00:12:31.667 --> 00:12:35.087
- So any time I’m doing an interview, 
I always try to ask

00:12:35.087 --> 00:12:37.339
people that know my guests about them,

00:12:37.339 --> 00:12:40.176
and what they would ask them, 
what they think of the person.

00:12:40.176 --> 00:12:43.220
So when I asked Kevin Love about 
what you have meant to his life,

00:12:43.220 --> 00:12:44.680
this was what he said to me.

00:12:44.680 --> 00:12:45.306
- Mhmm.

00:12:45.306 --> 00:12:49.018
- “DeMar opened the door for me, 
and at a time I needed it the most.

00:12:49.018 --> 00:12:52.062
I thank him and show love for 
him every time I see him now.

00:12:52.062 --> 00:12:55.566
It’s more than just a, ‘Hey, I’ve known you 
since high school’ brotherly hello.

00:12:55.566 --> 00:12:58.861
It’s more of a, ‘You helped me out of 
the darkness’ type of bond,

00:12:58.861 --> 00:13:00.571
whether he knows it or not.”

00:13:00.571 --> 00:13:01.697
- Kevin said that?

00:13:01.697 --> 00:13:01.989
- Yep.

00:13:01.989 --> 00:13:06.035
- Man, where you at, Kev? 
That’s a hug from me to you, Kev.

00:13:06.035 --> 00:13:09.163
No, Kev my man, like—
that meant a lot.

00:13:09.163 --> 00:13:12.792
Nobody never know what 
we go through as athletes,

00:13:12.792 --> 00:13:18.088
you know, so for me to open the door 
in my selfish moment of feeling how I felt,

00:13:18.088 --> 00:13:19.924
and, you know, just sayin’, “Fuck it,

00:13:19.924 --> 00:13:22.301
I’mma just go out and be straight up with this.”

00:13:22.301 --> 00:13:27.389
For him lookin’ at me in a light, 
like, I helped him out, that’s dope.

00:13:27.389 --> 00:13:30.559
- Yeah, and for the words that 
he used were so powerful—

00:13:30.559 --> 00:13:33.354
- Yeah.
- That you got him out of a darkness.

00:13:33.354 --> 00:13:38.275
- If we could do that for one another, 
imagine what we doin’ for everybody else.

00:13:38.275 --> 00:13:38.901
- Mhmm.

00:13:38.901 --> 00:13:40.277
- You know, we just settin’ the tone for that,

00:13:40.277 --> 00:13:44.156
and we really doin’ something that’s really inspiring.

00:13:44.156 --> 00:13:45.115
That’s definitely cool.

00:13:45.741 --> 00:13:49.620
- What helps you now get through depression?

00:13:49.620 --> 00:13:53.916
- My two daughters, setting the greatest example for them.

00:13:53.916 --> 00:13:57.962
The light that they look at me in is like I’m Superman.

00:13:57.962 --> 00:14:00.172
With that in the back of my mind in everything I do,

00:14:00.172 --> 00:14:03.884
it makes it easy to be motivated, 
to push, to go through the pain,

00:14:03.884 --> 00:14:07.221
to go through the tough times, 
to understand how to be better,

00:14:07.221 --> 00:14:07.763
you know, for them.

00:14:08.138 --> 00:14:08.889
There’s no beatin’ that.

00:14:08.889 --> 00:14:16.105
[♪♪♪]

00:14:16.105 --> 00:14:17.064
Yeah, this it for me.

